1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Kum.

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:04,200
I want to go public.

3
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:05,400
Is that a good idea, Anda?

4
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,200
Your family isn't okay with this, are they?

5
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:08,840
Anda.

6
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:10,760
Why did you come home so early?

7
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,920
You know what your dad is like lately.

8
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:18,280
Can you pretend you're hitting on me?

9
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:19,240
Okay.

10
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:20,120
I'll

11
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:20,760
hit

12
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:21,200
on

13
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:21,680
you.

14
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:24,000
Sheesh...

15
00:00:24,120 --> 00:00:25,720
Is my friend about to get into a relationship?

16
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:26,520
If that's the case,

17
00:00:26,520 --> 00:00:28,600
the rivalry between the two faculties is over.

18
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:29,880
Now they're two loving faculties.

19
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:31,160
I've got you this.

20
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:32,400
I think you'll like it.

21
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:37,680
Where did you get this?!

22
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:51,400
Hey...

23
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,320
Are those the freshmen?

24
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:55,880
Yeah.

25
00:00:56,040 --> 00:00:57,360
They probably just got back from camp.

26
00:00:58,400 --> 00:00:58,880
- See you.
- Let me talk to...

27
00:00:58,880 --> 00:00:59,720
That kid,

28
00:01:00,120 --> 00:01:01,200
what's his name?

29
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:02,240
It's Satang,

30
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:03,320
a first-year Automotive Engineering student.

31
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:08,039
Hello, hello.

32
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:13,000
How are things?

33
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:14,320
Was the camp fun?

34
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:15,560
It was.

35
00:01:16,080 --> 00:01:17,600
But I almost got my face burned off.

36
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:19,039
It was scorching hot.

37
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:21,000
I thought you'd be there, too.

38
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:22,240
Us, really?

39
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:23,440
How would we even make it?

40
00:01:23,440 --> 00:01:25,120
We already don't have time
to work on our project.

41
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:25,880
Gosh...

42
00:01:26,039 --> 00:01:27,720
It's just a project. What's to worry about?

43
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:28,880
You're just that cool, you know?

44
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:34,680
Jinna.

45
00:01:35,880 --> 00:01:37,280
I really like you.

46
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:39,880
What the hell?

47
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:41,400
That came out of nowhere.

48
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:42,880
No...

49
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:44,000
I mean,

50
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:45,880
you're my idol

51
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:50,440
in sports

52
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:51,400
and academics.

53
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:54,400
You play soccer, too?

54
00:01:54,479 --> 00:01:55,360
I do.

55
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:57,160
I played for my school.

56
00:01:57,160 --> 00:01:58,440
You sure you can handle it?

57
00:01:58,560 --> 00:01:59,600
I'm up for any challenge.

58
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,160
God damn.

59
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:02,880
Satang, right?

60
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:03,720
Yes.

61
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:04,680
My name's "Satang."

62
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:06,040
A girly name, right?

63
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:08,479
When I was little, I told my mom

64
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:09,759
I wanted another name,

65
00:02:09,759 --> 00:02:11,680
but she wanted to stick with
Thai currency names.

66
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:12,440
Why, though?

67
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:13,760
You've got a cool name.

68
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:15,160
Sounds like you'll make a fortune.

69
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:16,280
Tod,

70
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:18,320
what kind of currency

71
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,040
would I be?

72
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:20,880
"Euro?"

73
00:02:22,079 --> 00:02:22,640
Handsome.

74
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:24,600
Judging by your looks,

75
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:26,680
I'd say "bottle caps"

76
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:28,240
cause it sounds like "crap."

77
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:29,520
Damn you!

78
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:30,760
You and your foul mouth.

79
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:33,079
My older brother is also named
after a currency,

80
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:35,440
but it's obsolete now.

81
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:38,120
What currency is obsolete now?

82
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:41,160
His name is "Podduang."

83
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,320
He's a third-year student, just like you.

84
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,240
Podduang from
the Faculty of Sports and Health Science?

85
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:47,200
Right on the money.

86
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:48,880
You know him?

87
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,440
What, seriously?!

88
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:51,840
Podduang

89
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:53,160
is interning at the soccer club.

90
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:54,480
We know him.

91
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:55,880
Really?

92
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:57,880
Damn, you know him?

93
00:02:59,120 --> 00:03:00,120
Of course.

94
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:01,720
I know him well!

95
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:07,000
Podduang,

96
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:10,160
why didn't you tell me?

97
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:13,280
You get to be in the same club as Jinna,

98
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:15,120
and see him every day.

99
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:17,160
I would've joined too if I'd known.

100
00:03:18,880 --> 00:03:20,360
The internship is necessary.

101
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:22,079
I'm not passionate about soccer.

102
00:03:22,079 --> 00:03:23,320
No...

103
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:25,840
You know how hot Jinna is, right?

104
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:29,440
Just watching him play soccer

105
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:30,880
