00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:34,440
- Look.
- I'm going blind from it.

287
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:35,840
Always with the teasing, huh?

288
00:11:36,120 --> 00:11:37,240
Congratulations.

289
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:39,240
I told you you'd win the award either way.

290
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:41,840
Your name is all over
the damn media this year.

291
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:44,040
Isn't it because of the backlash?

292
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:44,840
- Hey.
- Oh?

293
00:11:45,440 --> 00:11:46,720
You're overthinking it.

294
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:49,080
Where there's love, there's hate.

295
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:50,840
That's just how it goes.

296
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:52,120
At least,

297
00:11:52,120 --> 00:11:54,640
there are more people
who love you than hate you

298
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:55,840
What is certain

299
00:11:56,520 --> 00:11:58,000
is that we love you the most.

300
00:11:58,840 --> 00:11:59,440
I'm gonna throw up.

301
00:11:59,440 --> 00:12:00,520
How could you say that?

302
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:02,000
So you do know how to say nice things.

303
00:12:02,160 --> 00:12:03,240
Of course.

304
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:07,040
The question is,
where should we celebrate tonight?

305
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:08,680
Not this again.

306
00:12:08,680 --> 00:12:10,040
Oh, you prick.

307
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:11,320
- Enough already.
- Watch it.

308
00:12:11,680 --> 00:12:12,840
So where are we celebrating?

309
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:13,840
Ask Kum to join us, too.

310
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:15,280
Well...

311
00:12:16,280 --> 00:12:17,560
A friend's friend's place, then.

312
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:19,320
I'll bring Kum there, too,

313
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:21,000
so I don't have to worry about paparazzi.

314
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:22,000
You're...

315
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:23,840
so lucky to have a good boyfriend.

316
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:25,440
Well, of course.

317
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,320
I’m already unlucky enough to have you.

318
00:12:27,320 --> 00:12:27,840
What?

319
00:12:27,840 --> 00:12:29,000
This damn celebrity.

320
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:30,320
You're getting on my nerves...

321
00:12:30,320 --> 00:12:31,840
- I'll kick your ass.
- Don't.

322
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:33,840
- Don't.
- Don't you dare.

323
00:12:33,840 --> 00:12:34,640
Don't.

324
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:50,840
Jeez,

325
00:12:50,840 --> 00:12:52,280
not going to say hi?

326
00:12:52,280 --> 00:12:54,840
We were talking the whole night.

327
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:55,840
Hey...

328
00:12:56,480 --> 00:12:58,640
Don't make it sound like that.

329
00:12:58,840 --> 00:13:00,680
We were just on the phone.

330
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:02,640
That's what I meant.

331
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:03,840
How did you interpret it?

332
00:13:07,040 --> 00:13:08,320
Where are you going after this?

333
00:13:08,640 --> 00:13:09,720
To my room, obviously.

334
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:11,040
Satang is waiting for me for dinner.

335
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:12,840
Oh, well...

336
00:13:13,840 --> 00:13:14,680
Never mind.

337
00:13:16,040 --> 00:13:17,440
Tonight, I'm drinking with my friends.

338
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:21,520
Go on, then.

339
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:22,840
Why are you telling me that?

340
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:25,360
Just letting you know

341
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:26,840
in case I don't call you.

342
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:30,080
No need to wait for me,

343
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:30,840
understand?

344
00:13:31,680 --> 00:13:32,720
Who says I do?

345
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:35,600
Are you full of yourself?

346
00:13:38,480 --> 00:13:39,840
You're talking nonsense.

347
00:13:40,360 --> 00:13:42,480
You're wasting my time here.

348
00:13:50,840 --> 00:13:51,640
Lost...

349
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,240
You've lost it.

350
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:55,520
You like my friend that much, don't you?

351
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:57,840
That much, yeah.

352
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:05,320
Alright, alright.

353
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:06,400
Cheers

354
00:14:06,560 --> 00:14:08,720
to my rising star!

355
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:09,400
Alright, cheers.

356
00:14:09,400 --> 00:14:11,320
Yeah.

357
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:14,200
You just love calling me
by my award title, huh?

358
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:16,120
It's the opposite of the state
I'm in right now,

359
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:17,600
that's why I'm drinking here with you.

360
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:20,040
The series that got put on hold...

361
00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:20,920
Gosh!

362
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:21,920
It can stay that way.

363
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:23,400
Your ship partner's a freak.

364
00:14:23,560 --> 00:14:25,360
All he cares about is the trend.

365
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:27,640
On that day,
when he came to our faculty,

366
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:30,320
he was lucky Jinna and I
didn't beat him up.

367
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:33,440
Try brushing it off.

368
00:14:33,720 --> 00:14:37,240
Announcing like that
means you respect your loved one,

369
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:38,720
your fans,

370
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:40,440
and yourself.

371
00:14:41,160 --> 00:14:41,720
It's true.

372
00:14:42,080 --> 00:14:43,400
Winning the award

373
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:45,040
already proves that

374
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:47,240
the community accepts you.

375
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:49,480
In the end, no matter who you are,

376
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:51,600
we're all human, Anda.

377
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:55,000
Right, right, right.

378
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:57,320
I'm trying to stop thinking about it.

379
00:14:57,840 --> 00:14:59,240
But you know that, don't you?

380
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:02,240
Even though the whole world accepts me...

381
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:04,240
my family...

382
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:08,080
Enough of that, Anda...

383
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:10,000
Let's stop talking about serious stuff.

384
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:12,040
We're here to celebrate, aren't we?

385
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:13,360
You're right.

386
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:14,920
You guys,

387
00:15:14,920 --> 00:15:16,160
why are you all so serious?

388
00:15:16,320 --> 00:15:18,080
Come on, a toast.

389
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:20,360
I won't let you off until you're hammered.

390
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:21,720
Alright.

391
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,720
You're drunk. Take it easy already.

392
00:15:32,320 --> 00:15:33,280
Jinna...

393
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:35,720
why don't you find yourself a partner?

394
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:38,120
Just look at mine,

395
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:41,280
he's so handsome and good...

396
00:15:41,720 --> 00:15:43,160
Are you not envious?

397
00:15:43,520 --> 00:15:45,040
What the hell?

398
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:46,720
Are you showing off your partner now?

399
00:15:47,320 --> 00:15:48,560
I'm not.

400
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:50,360
I'm serious.

401
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:51,920
I'm

402
00:15:51,920 --> 00:15:53,280
so damn fortunate

403
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:54,720
to have Kum as my boyfriend.

404
00:15:59,360 --> 00:16:00,240
Do you think...

405
00:16:01,280 --> 00:16:03,720
I'd be able to go on
if I broke up with him?

406
00:16:05,440 --> 00:16:07,000
Why do you ask that, Anda?

407
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:08,360
Well...

408
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:09,440
I'm thinking about

409
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:10,720
the worst-case scenario.

410
00:16:13,240 --> 00:16:15,280
I'll never break up with you,

411
00:16:16,200 --> 00:16:17,720
no matter what.

412
00:16:22,240 --> 00:16:23,480
You're so sweet...

413
00:16:31,040 --> 00:16:33,880
You pass out every
damn time you take a sip.

414
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:36,160
If it weren't for me,
you'd probably be missing a kidney now.

415
00:16:36,160 --> 00:16:38,400
Take care of me until old age, then.

416
00:16:39,240 --> 00:16:41,440
- There, tell that to your boyfriend.
- Jinna.

417
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:43,520
I'm gonna go back to drinking now.

418
00:16:44,160 --> 00:16:45,040
Thanks, Jinna.

419
00:16:45,280 --> 00:16:46,520
I'll take it from here.

420
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:48,520
He might throw up in the car, alright?

421
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,280
Come, Anda.

422
00:16:51,520 --> 00:16:52,360
Let's go home.

423
00:16:52,520 --> 00:16:53,520
Careful now.

424
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:54,760
There are steps.

425
00:16:55,400 --> 00:16:56,040
Come on.

426
00:16:57,520 --> 00:16:58,320
Take a step.

427
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:01,520
Slowly.

428
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:06,400
[Stadium]

429
00:17:09,520 --> 00:17:10,599
Tod and Art?

430
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:11,319
Where are they?

431
00:17:12,040 --> 00:17:13,319
They're talking to a professor.

432
00:17:13,520 --> 00:17:14,319
They'll be here soon.

433
00:17:15,640 --> 00:17:17,599
I have to leave a bit early, though.

434
00:17:17,599 --> 00:17:19,000
Need to take care of something.

435
00:17:19,520 --> 00:17:20,319
Mm.

436
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:22,640
Go and rest up.

437
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:26,000
We're worried about you.

438
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:36,920
Podduang.

439
00:17:38,080 --> 00:17:39,280
Do you need help?

440
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:41,320
It's okay, Anda.

441
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:42,480
I'm used to it now.

442
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:49,600
I think...

443
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:52,280
I need to go now.

444
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:54,600
Tell Tod and Art for me, okay?

445
00:17:55,400 --> 00:17:56,040
Right.

446
00:17:56,320 --> 00:17:57,000
Don't worry.

447
00:17:57,600 --> 00:17:58,600
Stay safe.

448
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:01,000
Bye.

449
00:18:02,600 --> 00:18:03,400
Anda!

450
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:08,240
Get some proper rest if you're sleepy.

451
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:10,040
Don't sleep in the car.

452
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:15,000
Okay.

453
00:18:39,840 --> 00:18:41,040
Why do you keep staring?

454
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:42,000
No, well...

455
00:18:42,280 --> 00:18:43,600
You know Jinna, right?

456
00:18:44,360 --> 00:18:47,040
Of course,
you've been talking about him daily.

457
00:18:47,360 --> 00:18:49,000
No, not like that.

458
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:50,240
I mean...

459
00:18:50,600 --> 00:18:51,600
You know each other,

460
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:53,320
don't you?

461
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:55,280
Well, of course we do.

462
00:18:55,280 --> 00:18:57,160
I'm an intern at the soccer club.

463
00:18:58,400 --> 00:19:00,000
And... like...

464
00:19:00,920 --> 00:19:02,400
How well do you know each other?

465
00:19:04,240 --> 00:19:05,040
Is it more than just friends?

466
00:19:06,120 --> 00:19:06,880
You know what?

467
00:19:07,040 --> 00:19:09,000
Just get to the point, Satang.

468
00:19:10,240 --> 00:19:11,600
No, well...

469
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:13,880
There's a rumor going around
at the university

470
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:15,600
that...

471
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:18,600
Jinna is hitting on
a Sports and Health Science student.

472
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:20,320
I just want to know

473
00:19:20,480 --> 00:19:21,600
who it is.

474
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:24,760
My friends in the faculty say

475
00:19:25,640 --> 00:19:26,560
that...

476
00:19:27,840 --> 00:19:29,440
he's been hitting on you.

477
00:19:33,240 --> 00:19:33,880
Right.

478
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:34,720
Listen up.

479
00:19:34,720 --> 00:19:35,800
Jinna and I are just...

480
00:19:35,800 --> 00:19:37,080
[Jinna Ronnarak is calling...]

481
00:19:37,080 --> 00:19:37,920
I knew it!

482
00:19:38,320 --> 00:19:40,440
Wow, you two are video calling each other.

483
00:19:41,160 --> 00:19:42,080
Say it and make my night.

484
00:19:42,080 --> 00:19:43,960
You really had to call
at the perfect time.

485
00:19:43,960 --> 00:19:45,840
If this is nothing important,

486
00:19:46,240 --> 00:19:48,440
I'll scold you like there's no tomorrow!

487
00:19:48,440 --> 00:19:49,200
Just you wait!

488
00:19:51,640 --> 00:19:53,000
Miss you...

489
00:19:55,920 --> 00:19:56,760
Aren't you...

490
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:58,200
too invested?

491
00:19:58,640 --> 00:20:00,400
This is nothing but a play.

492
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:01,400
Don't forget that.

493
00:20:04,040 --> 00:20:05,000
Why?

494
00:20:05,640 --> 00:20:06,800
Why are we only pretending?

495
00:20:07,480 --> 00:20:09,400
I told you I hate pretending.

496
00:20:09,840 --> 00:20:10,400
Why?

497
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:12,000
If I actually wanted to hit on you,

498
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:13,600
that wouldn't be okay?

499
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:15,000
You're...

500
00:20:15,560 --> 00:20:16,760
kidding me, right?

501
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:22,000
You think?

502
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:23,920
God!

503
00:20:23,920 --> 00:20:25,600
Why can't you just answer me directly?

504
00:20:25,600 --> 00:20:27,240
Why do you always
answer me with a question?

505
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:27,960
On top of that,

506
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:30,400
you're making the act feel so real.

507
00:20:30,520 --> 00:20:31,760
I'm simple-minded, Jinna.

508
00:20:32,880 --> 00:20:34,400
Why do you have to make me feel things?

509
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:36,920
Gotcha!

510
00:20:36,920 --> 00:20:37,920
You're talking to Jinna.

511
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:43,400
Huh?

512
00:20:43,680 --> 00:20:44,400
What do you mean?

513
00:20:44,400 --> 00:20:44,880
What?!

514
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:45,920
You finished dinner already?

515
00:20:45,920 --> 00:20:47,200
Downed the whole thing.

516
00:20:47,760 --> 00:20:48,840
Don't be shy.

517
00:20:49,520 --> 00:20:50,280
It's normal.

518
00:20:50,280 --> 00:20:51,160
A grain of rice is on your face.

519
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:51,960
Is it?

520
00:20:52,240 --> 00:20:52,840
Yeah.

521
00:20:54,120 --> 00:20:55,400
Wash your mouth first.

522
00:20:55,720 --> 00:20:56,200
No, but...

523
00:20:56,200 --> 00:20:57,720
you're probably more than just friends...

524
00:20:57,720 --> 00:20:58,960
video calling like that.

525
00:20:58,960 --> 00:21:00,400
Are you deaf or something?

526
00:21:00,680 --> 00:21:01,600
You still haven't finished yours.

527
00:21:01,600 --> 00:21:02,720
Huh?

528
00:21:02,920 --> 00:21:03,560
I'm full already...

529
00:21:03,560 --> 00:21:04,000
Hey.

530
00:21:04,240 --> 00:21:04,720
Hey!

531
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:07,400
You're full of secrets.

532
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:08,000
What secrets?

533
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,400
I don't have any.

534
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:09,800
You're lying.

535
00:22:11,920 --> 00:22:13,200
Come to think of it,

536
00:22:13,200 --> 00:22:15,040
Anda is quite talented, honey.

537
00:22:15,320 --> 00:22:17,200
I've heard that for the award ceremony,

538
00:22:17,440 --> 00:22:19,840
only big-name actors

539
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:21,000
were invited.

540
00:22:21,720 --> 00:22:22,600
Isn't that right, dear?

541
00:22:23,040 --> 00:22:23,800
That's right.

542
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:26,040
There are...

543
00:22:26,760 --> 00:22:27,920
several award categories.

544
00:22:28,760 --> 00:22:29,600
Really?

545
00:22:34,840 --> 00:22:37,000
I just want this award to prove

546
00:22:37,920 --> 00:22:38,760
that...

547
00:22:39,160 --> 00:22:41,560
I'm doing well on
the path I've chosen, Dad.

548
00:22:43,560 --> 00:22:44,560
I wonder

549
00:22:45,320 --> 00:22:46,640
how prestigious

550
00:22:46,640 --> 00:22:48,240
your damn award really is?

551
00:22:50,120 --> 00:22:52,320
Were you defending the country?

552
00:22:53,320 --> 00:22:54,600
In truth,

553
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:57,320
it's just an award for showbiz people.

554
00:22:57,520 --> 00:22:58,680
Worse yet...

555
00:23:01,320 --> 00:23:03,600
they're all cut from the same cloth.

556
00:23:04,480 --> 00:23:05,320
Honey...

557
00:23:05,680 --> 00:23:06,600
When the hell

558
00:23:07,160 --> 00:23:10,040
are you going to stop embarrassing me?

559
00:23:11,040 --> 00:23:14,320
Why can't you just be on the right track
like Itti, your older brother?

560
00:23:14,760 --> 00:23:15,640
For Itti

561
00:23:16,800 --> 00:23:19,320
to rise to such a high rank in the police,

562
00:23:20,040 --> 00:23:22,040
he had to achieve a lot.

563
00:23:22,440 --> 00:23:23,520
That's more like it!

564
00:23:23,840 --> 00:23:27,320
That’s what makes it a profession
worthy of respect and pride.

565
00:23:30,520 --> 00:23:33,120
So those are the only professions
worth being proud of?

566
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:36,560
Do other professions have
no prestige or honor at all?!

567
00:23:36,880 --> 00:23:39,040
Am I that worthless

568
00:23:39,480 --> 00:23:40,960
for not fighting a criminal?!

569
00:23:43,400 --> 00:23:45,800
You're standing here arguing with me nonstop,

570
00:23:45,800 --> 00:23:48,520
and you actually expect me
to be proud of your stupid award?!

571
00:23:50,760 --> 00:23:52,000
Do you know that

572
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:53,560
you are...

573
00:23:53,560 --> 00:23:55,320
the problem in this family?!

574
00:23:55,320 --> 00:23:56,320
